<!--
EURAD-2 MS33 Theoretical Benchmarking — Model IV
Clay-pellets interaction, homogenization in dry density
BGR / DSM native hierarchical vdW-augmented model

Geometry: 50mm diam × 70mm height axisymmetric cylinder — CONCENTRIC (spec Fig4pellets.jpg):
  Bentonite core  (medium id=0): r=0–0.015m (Ø30 mm), z=0–0.070m (full height)  (MaterialID=0)
  Pellet annulus  (medium id=1): r=0.015–0.025m,       z=0–0.070m (full height)  (MaterialID=1)
  Mesh ms33_pellets_concentric_r25_h70.vtu (2026-09-08): the SAME 1066 nodes / 1000 quads (1 mm x 1.75 mm)
  as ms33_pellets_r25_h70.vtu with MaterialIDs relabelled by cell-centroid radius (r < 15 mm -> 0, else 1;
  600 clay / 400 pellet cells); boundary meshes unchanged (same node ids).
  SPEC-CONFORMANCE FIX 1 (Vinay 2026-09-08 "approve all five, run them as one campaign";
  audits/2026-09-08_spec_conformance_full/AUDIT.md §4 + VERIFY_refutation row 1, five independent routes:
  Fig4pellets.jpg "Clay 30 mm" core inside the "Pellets" annulus; AMPHOS21.tex L327; UCLM.tex L430;
  CTU-CU.tex L422 (6x20 + 4x20 radial split); CIMNE 1.15 g/cm3 = 0.36*1.6 + 0.64*0.9).
  HISTORY (gen 1-4, through 2026-08-31, SUPERSEDED, kept per CLAUDE.md 6.3): the deck used
  ms33_pellets_r25_h70.vtu, a STACKED layout — block r=0–0.025 / z=0.035–0.070 over pellets
  r=0–0.025 / z=0–0.035 — which is NOT the spec's geometry (clay hydrated only through the pellets,
  clay volume fraction 0.50 instead of 0.36, no equivalent of either prescribed probe).

Bentonite: rho_d=1600 kg/m³, phi0=0.424460, LIVE K(rho_d) table (2026-08-18; was fixed
  K=103879 J/kg, Dixon 2023 Fig.1, EMDD=rho_d, 14.161 MPa; supersedes Villar 29999.25)
Pellets:   rho_d=900  kg/m³, phi0=0.676259, LIVE K(rho_d) table; SAME table as the
  bentonite zone (2026-08-18, Vinay: "share the Dixon table for the pellet too"; the
  pellet zone's own dry density trajectory measures 900 -> ~1045-1160 kg/m3 by 200d
  across the permeability sweep, i.e. it COMPACTS under the swelling block above it,
  moving meaningfully into the table's 900-1400 interpolation interval). RETIRES the
  former dedicated fixed K=20600 J/kg (Dixon-range EXTRAPOLATION to user-set target
  sigma_sat(rho_d=900)=0.400 MPa, Vinay 2026-06-08; kept for lineage below).
  Pellet k0 from Kozeny-Carman with k_ref=5.6e-21 m² at phi_ref=0.42

Official benchmark spec (MSXX §Model IV):
  Initial suction = 100 MPa for both zones
  Same hydration BC as reference configuration (bottom suction ramp)
  Both zones use same 200-day simulation
-->
