  <!-- GUARDRAIL §12.5 audit (2026-08-18, Vinay-approved): intrinsic permeability set
       to 160x the deck's Kozeny-Carman base 5.8703e-21 m^2 = 9.39248e-19 m^2 clay
       (pellet = 10x clay = 9.39248e-18 m^2, Vinay 2026-06-08 rule unchanged), the
       SAME absolute permeability as ms33_modelIII_gapswitch.prj /
       ms33_modelVII_freeswelling.prj. SUPERSEDES the 20x value 1.17406e-19 m^2 clay
       set 2026-06-09 under fixed-K: after Vinay's ruling that BOTH zones report live
       K(rho_d) from the shared Dixon table (2026-08-18, "share the Dixon table for
       the pellet too and redo it"), the equilibration margin needed re-measurement;
       re-verified via a {20x,160x,320x,640x} parallel sweep at the bentonite-block
       top probe (r=0,z=0.070) and pellet-zone bottom probe (r=0,z=0), t=200d:
           20x:  sig_top=4.29482 MPa, sig_bot=0.56665 MPa (short of the plateau)
           160x: sig_top=4.38664 MPa, sig_bot=0.65784 MPa
           320x: sig_top=4.37066 MPa, sig_bot=0.66512 MPa
           640x: sig_top=4.34767 MPa, sig_bot=0.66184 MPa
       160x/320x/640x agree to within ~1% of each other (k0-independent) and each
       individually plateaus EXACTLY flat from 100d to 200d (t_eq well under 100d,
       >=100-day margin); a dramatic improvement over the PRE-pellet-live-K sweep
       (same day, DSM/AGENTS.md entry 20), where the bottom probe was still moving
       5-10% between 320x and 640x with no clean k0-independent plateau even at 640x.
       The earlier non-convergence was diagnosed as the fixed pellet K=20600 fighting
       the softening live-K bentonite driver on a much longer coupled timescale; making
       the pellet zone ALSO live (weaker driver at its low initial density) resolved
       it. Chose 160x to match the suite-wide III/VII convention (one permeability
       number, not a per-model special case). -->
