                       times in it.  The LIVE macro retention property, IDENTICAL in both media
                       (MaterialID 0 block and MaterialID 1 pellet zone), is
                       <type>SaturationTuller</type>, with
                           area_factor_tuller           = 1.0
                           pore_area_shapefactor_tuller = 0.8584073464102069
                           characteristic_pore_size     = 1e-5   m
                           surface_tension              = 0.0715 N/m
                           cavitation_pressure          = 1.4e8  Pa
                       Source status, per parameter: cavitation_pressure = 1.4e8 Pa is Or and
                       Tuller (2002), WRR 38(5) 1061.  The Tuller pore geometry
                       (area_factor_tuller, pore_area_shapefactor_tuller,
                       characteristic_pore_size) and surface_tension are carried over from the
                       parity PRJs of the dsm_mfront_hierarchical branch, as the inline comment
                       at the property itself records ("parity-branch params").  A parity or
                       port branch is NOT one of §12.1's six allowed source families
                       (Beacon / EPFL / Dixon / Villar / EURAD-MS / FEBEX); it is recorded here
